---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="evaluerBench | Josh Oney">
	<section class="project-view">
		<div class="project-header">
			<h1>evaluerBench</h1>
			<a href="https://github.com/joshoney/evaluerBench" target="_blank" class="github-btn">View on GitHub ↗</a>
		</div>
		
		<div class="content-grid">
			<div class="text-block">
				<h2>The Need for Telemetry</h2>
				<p>When working with Local LLMs, understanding <em>why</em> an agent failed is just as important as knowing <em>that</em> it failed. I built evaluerBench to parse, visualize, and compare complex AI evaluation data in real time.</p>
				
				<h2>Architectural Choices</h2>
				<p>The dashboard focuses on high-density information display. By adopting an LCARS-inspired matrix grid and detailed side-by-side comparison views, I can quickly scan pass/fail rates, identify timeout regressions, and even launch fully interactive HTML/JS artifacts generated by the model directly within an iframe sandbox.</p>
				
				<h2>Tech Stack</h2>
				<ul>
					<li><strong>Framework:</strong> Astro</li>
					<li><strong>Styling:</strong> Vanilla CSS (CSS Variables, Flexbox/Grid)</li>
					<li><strong>Data:</strong> JSON serialized telemetry blobs</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>
</Layout>

<style>
	.project-view {
		max-width: 900px;
		padding: 20px 0;
	}

	.project-header {
		display: flex;
		justify-content: space-between;
		align-items: center;
		border-bottom: 3px solid var(--lcars-blue);
		padding-bottom: 20px;
		margin-bottom: 30px;
	}

	.project-header h1 {
		font-size: 2.8rem;
		margin: 0;
		color: #fff;
		font-family: var(--font-sans);
		font-weight: 800;
	}

	.github-btn {
		background: var(--lcars-blue);
		color: #000;
		padding: 10px 20px;
		font-family: var(--font-mono);
		font-weight: bold;
		border-radius: 4px;
		transition: filter 0.15s, transform 0.1s;
	}

	.github-btn:hover {
		filter: brightness(1.2);
		transform: scale(1.02);
	}

	.content-grid {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: 30px;
	}

	.text-block h2 {
		color: var(--lcars-blue);
		font-family: var(--font-mono);
		font-size: 1.4rem;
		margin-bottom: 12px;
		letter-spacing: 1px;
	}

	.text-block p {
		font-size: 1.1rem;
		color: var(--text-main);
		margin-bottom: 25px;
		line-height: 1.7;
	}

	.text-block ul {
		padding-left: 20px;
		color: var(--text-muted);
		font-size: 1.1rem;
		line-height: 1.8;
	}
	
	.text-block li {
		margin-bottom: 8px;
	}
</style>
